Does anybody know literary details about Grayswandir? It seems to be
originating from Roger Zelazny's novel as quoted in Nethack's database:

     Why had I been wearing Grayswandir?  Would another weapon have
     affected a Logrus-ghost as strongly?  Had it really been my
     father, then, who had brought me here?  And had he felt I might
     need the extra edge his weapon could provide?  I wanted to
     think so, to believe that he had been more than a Pattern-ghost.
             [ Knight of Shadows, by Roger Zelazny ]

What I am interested in is the background and some details about the
effect of hallucination resistance that might be described in the book.

I am asking because in another book I am currently reading there is some
similar effect described; a wolpertinger[*] got rid of his dulled senses
that he had from his ethanol abuse by wielding some epee (sword).

[*] Don't ask what a wolpertinger is; apparently some species missing in
Nethack, unfortunately! (Though you'll find some pictures in google.)

